Note that this implementation assumes a simplified model of the sun's position and does not take into account other factors like atmospheric refraction, cloud cover, or time-of-day variations. Additionally, it does not account for non-solar noon times in the Northern or Southern Hemispheres.

The `calculateSunset` function returns the time of sunset based on the input date, latitude, and longitude. It assumes a simplified model where the sun sets at the horizon and uses the "North" direction as the standard. The returned string is formatted to display the hour and minutes since solar noon (i.e., sunset) in 24-hour format.

Please note that this implementation may not accurately reflect real-world conditions or atmospheric effects, which are essential for accurate time-of-day calculations in a practical application.
